WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.376
Every number on a ride starts as a few bytes from the bike. Telo Ride now reads

00:00:07.376 --> 00:00:07.979
them.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:17.880
A D2 frame carries the resistance. F0, D2, 01, 0C, CF is level twelve.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:26.697
A D1 frame carries cadence, big-endian in bytes nine and ten. Zero, fifty hex is

00:00:26.697 --> 00:00:27.829
eighty rpm.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:36.489
A frame that's too short, doesn't start with F0, is of an unknown type, or is a D0,

00:00:36.489 --> 00:00:38.584
is ignored, never an error.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.988
An FTMS bike's flags say which fields follow. Speed, cadence, power and heart rate

00:00:46.988 --> 00:00:49.995
are read; the rest are skipped by size.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:57.003
An Echelon reports no speed or power, so they're estimated. Eighty rpm is thirty

00:00:57.003 --> 00:00:58.582
kilometres an hour.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:07.421
An FTMS bike's own power and speed are used as they are. A field it leaves out falls

00:01:07.421 --> 00:01:09.808
back to the estimate, or a dash.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.042
If cadence stops for five seconds, cadence and power go blank, rather than show a

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:19.052
number that's no longer true.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:28.063
Still to come: slice 3.2 puts these numbers on screen, with distance and energy, and

00:01:28.063 --> 00:01:29.861
proves them end to end.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.561
Home doesn't change yet, at any width. The numbers wait in the engine for the ride

00:01:37.561 --> 00:01:38.315
screens.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.928
What the tests prove: forty-five new unit tests, one per row of the requirements,

00:01:47.928 --> 00:01:49.792
and every spec still green.

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:58.164
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:03.021
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:04.692
every hill and interval.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:10.215
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:02:10.215 --> 00:02:15.663
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:18.653
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:18.998 --> 00:02:21.491
A custom workout lives under Profile.
